    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.18.4</title>
      <pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:48:18 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>21804</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.18.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Sign in to your Squeak account in Settings &gt; Account (Zoho, Google or email). This Mac then appears in your account, and your iPhone or browser signed in to the same account joins it without a code. You're told each time, with Revoke; "Ask before adding my own devices" brings the code back.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.18.3</h4><ul><li>A browser signed in to your Squeak account can ask to be added without a QR code (approve it in Settings &gt; Channels, comparing the code), and Settings shows the account this Mac is linked to, with Unlink.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.18.2</h4><ul><li>A web guest who signs in with Zoho, Google or email shows on the join request with their verified email, so you know who you are letting into a pond.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
      <enclosure url="https://sibhimanyu.github.io/squeak/download/Squeak-2.18.4.dmg" length="69509055" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="S9o9L4XnXhWBiF665rVh20GljH30Ei78s56vy4+BE0cMpu9NS9Dzolfazf0/rJcgReFs9EnpKRu+bHa65dXhBg==" />
    </item>
